    <string name="charm_flavor_1">A tiny bell cast from morning dew. It rings only when nobody listens.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_2">Warm to the touch at noon, cool again by dusk.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_3">Four leaves tied so tightly the knot never slips.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_4">Pressed by the bees themselves, or so the meadow claims.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_5">Woven from the first barley of the season.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_6">It hums the tune the larks sing above the hill.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_7">An acorn dipped in amber, heavy with slow summers.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_8">Spiky, stubborn and strangely lucky.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_9">Brass wings that catch every stray glint of gold.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_10">A full moon beaten flat and hung on a cord.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_11">A fern frond gilded leaf by leaf over one long night.</string>
    <string name="charm_flavor_12">The meadow keeps one heart. You just found it.</string>

